Exceptions: parts of this repository under other licenses

- qemu/patches/: changes to QEMU, GPL-2.0-or-later (each new file says so in
  its SPDX line), as QEMU itself is GPL-2.0. The QEMU binaries in the VS Code
  extension are built from QEMU v11.1.2 plus these patches.

- examples/mplab/*/firmware/src/config/ and the MPLAB X project files beside
  them: generated by Microchip's MPLAB Code Configurator (Harmony CSP) and
  under Microchip's license as stated in each file's header.
  examples/mplab/*/firmware/src/packs/: copies of Arm CMSIS (Apache-2.0) and
  Microchip device pack headers (Apache-2.0), as MPLAB places them.
  firmware/src/main.c of each example is MIT as above.

- tools/pp_web/clicks/*/top.png and tools/pp_web/boards/*/top.png: artwork
  rendered from the board makers' published 2D/3D design files
  (MikroElektronika for the Click boards, Microchip for the evaluation
  boards). Board names, logos and silkscreen belong to their owners.

- devices/*.json and the generated register tables: derived from Microchip
  device pack ATDF files, which are Apache-2.0. The packs themselves are not
  in this repository; scripts/fetch_packs.py downloads them.

This is a personal project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored or endorsed
by Microchip Technology Inc., MikroElektronika or the QEMU project. Product
names are trademarks of their owners and are used only to say which hardware
is being simulated.
